.TH authpf-api-cli(1) - Command-line tool for authpf-api server and client operations
.SH NAME
\fBauthpf-api-cli\fP — Command-line tool for managing authpf-api server and performing client operations

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBauthpf-api-cli\fR [\fB--config\fR FILE] [\fB--verbose\fR] [\fBCOMMAND\fR] [\fBOPTIONS\fR]
.IP \(bu 2
\fBauthpf-api-cli auth\fR [\fBlogin|logout|status\fR]
.IP \(bu 2
\fBauthpf-api-cli authpf\fR [\fBactivate|deactivate|status\fR]
.IP \(bu 2
\fBauthpf-api-cli user\fR [\fBcreate|modify|delete|list\fR]
.IP \(bu 2
\fBauthpf-api-cli config\fR [\fBshow\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBauthpf-api-cli\fP is a command-line tool for managing the \fBauthpf-api\fP server and performing client operations. It can be used both on the server (for user and pf anchor management) and on the client (for authentication and anchor loading).

.PP
The tool provides functionality for:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAuthentication\fP: Login/logout and manage JWT tokens for secure API access
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRule Management\fP: Activate and deactivate PF user anchors with configurable timeouts
.IP \(bu 2
\fBConfiguration\fP: Check and validate server configuration
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUser Management\fP: Create, modify, and delete users with secure password hashing
.IP \(bu 2
\fBStatus Monitoring\fP: Check server and client status, view active sessions and loaded anchors

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--config\fP \fIfile\fP
Path to the configuration file. Defaults to \fB~/.authpf-api-cli/config\fR if not set.

.TP
\fB--verbose\fP, \fB-v\fP
Enable verbose output for debugging purposes.

.TP
\fB--help\fP, \fB-h\fP
Display help information and exit.

.TP
\fB--version\fP
Display version information and exit.

.SH COMMANDS
.SS auth
Authentication and session management

.PP
\fBauth login\fP
  Authenticate with the authpf-api server and obtain a JWT token.

.PP
\fBOptions:\fP
.TP
\fB--server\fP \fIURL\fP
URL of the authpf-api server (e.g., https://api.example.com). Required for first login.

.TP
\fB--username\fP \fIUSERNAME\fP
Username for authentication. Required for first login.

.TP
\fB--password\fP \fIPASSWORD\fP
Password for authentication. Required for first login. If not provided, will prompt interactively.

.TP
\fB--cacert\fP \fIFILE\fP, \fB-c\fP \fIFILE\fP
Path to a custom CA certificate file for HTTPS connections with self-signed certificates.

.TP
\fB--insecure\fP
Skip TLS certificate verification (not recommended for production).

.SS auth logout
Logout from the authpf-api server and remove the stored JWT token.

.SS auth status
Display the current authentication status and token information.

.SS authpf
PF anchor management

.SS authpf activate
Activate pf rules for the authenticated user.

.PP
\fBOptions:\fP
.TP
\fB--timeout\fP \fITIME\fP, \fB-t\fP \fITIME\fP
Override the default timeout for rule activation (e.g., 30m, 1h, 2h). Default is configured on the server.

.TP
\fB--username\fP \fIUSERNAME\fP, \fB-u\fP \fIUSERNAME\fP
Activate rules for another user (requires appropriate permissions).

.SS authpf deactivate
Deactivate pf rules for the authenticated user.

.PP
\fBOptions:\fP
.TP
\fBusername\fP \fIUSERNAME\fP, \fB-u\fP \fIUSERNAME\fP
Deactivate rules for another user (requires appropriate permissions).

.TP
\fBall\fP
Deactivate all activated rules (admin only).

.SS authpf status
Display the status of activated pf rules.

.PP
\fBOptions:\fP
.TP
\fBall\fP
Display status of all activated rules (admin only).

.SS user
User management (server-side)

.SS user create
Create a new user on the authpf-api server.

.PP
\fBOptions:\fP
.TP
\fBusername\fP \fIUSERNAME\fP
Username for the new user. Required.

.TP
\fBpassword\fP \fIPASSWORD\fP
Password for the new user. Required. If not provided, will prompt interactively.

.TP
\fBrole\fP \fIROLE\fP
User role: \fBuser\fR or \fBadmin\fR\&. Default is \fBuser\fR\&.

.SS user modify
Modify an existing user on the authpf-api server.

.PP
\fBOptions:\fP
.TP
\fBusername\fP \fIUSERNAME\fP
Username of the user to modify. Required.

.TP
\fBpassword\fP \fIPASSWORD\fP
New password for the user. If not provided, password remains unchanged.

.TP
\fBrole\fP \fIROLE\fP
New role for the user: \fBuser\fR or \fBadmin\fR\&.

.SS user delete
Delete a user from the authpf-api server.

.PP
\fBOptions:\fP
.TP
\fBusername\fP \fIUSERNAME\fP
Username of the user to delete. Required.

.SS user list
List all users on the authpf-api server.

.SS config
Configuration management

.SS config show
Display the current server configuration.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBAUTHPF_API_SERVER\fP
URL of the authpf-api server. Overrides the configured server value.

.TP
\fBAUTHPF_API_USERNAME\fP
Username for authentication. Overrides the configured username.

.TP
\fBAUTHPF_API_PASSWORD\fP
Password for authentication. Overrides the configured password.

.TP
\fBAUTHPF_API_TOKEN\fP
JWT token for authentication. Overrides the stored token.

.TP
\fBAUTHPF_API_CACERT\fP
Path to a custom CA certificate file.

.TP
\fBAUTHPF_API_INSECURE\fP
Skip TLS certificate verification if set to \fBtrue\fR\&.

.TP
\fBAUTHPF_API_AUTHPF_USERNAME\fP
Default authpf username for operations.

.TP
\fBAUTHPF_API_AUTHPF_TIMEOUT\fP
Default timeout for authpf rule activation.

.SH CONFIGURATION
\fBauthpf-api-cli\fP is configured via a YAML configuration file, typically located at \fB~/.authpf-api-cli/config\fR\&. The configuration file stores:
.IP \(bu 2
API server URL
.IP \(bu 2
JWT token (automatically stored after login)
.IP \(bu 2
CA certificate path for HTTPS connections

.PP
\fBExample configuration file:\fP

.EX
api:
  server: https://api.example.com
  token: ""
  cacert: ""
  insecure: false
.EE

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBLogin to API and get Token\fP
authpf-api-cli auth login --server https://api.example.com --username john --password mypassword

authpf-api-cli auth login --server https://api.example.com --username john --password mypassword -c ca-root.crt

.TP
\fBLogout from API\fP
authpf-api-cli auth logout

.TP
\fBShow Auth Status\fP
authpf-api-cli auth status

.TP
\fBActivate AuthPF Anchor\fP
authpf-api-cli authpf activate

authpf-api-cli authpf activate -t 1h

authpf-api-cli authpf activate -u user2

.TP
\fBDeactivate Anchor\fP
authpf-api-cli authpf deactivate

authpf-api-cli authpf deactivate -u user2

authpf-api-cli authpf deactivate --all

.TP
\fBShow Anchor Status (activated)\fP
authpf-api-cli authpf status

authpf-api-cli authpf status --all

.TP
\fBCreate API User\fP
authpf-api-cli user create --username john --password mypassword --role user

authpf-api-cli user create --username admin1 --password adminpass --role admin

.TP
\fBModify API User\fP
authpf-api-cli user modify --username john --password newpassword

authpf-api-cli user modify --username john --role admin

.TP
\fBRemove API User\fP
authpf-api-cli user delete --username john

.TP
\fBList API Users\fP
authpf-api-cli user list

.TP
\fBShow current API Config\fP
authpf-api-cli config show

.SS Typical AuthPF User Workflow
.EX
# Step 1: Login to the server (only required for first time)
authpf-api-cli auth login --server https://api.example.com --username alice --password pass123

# To get a new token (if already configured server and username/password)
authpf-api-cli auth login

# Step 2: Check login status
authpf-api-cli auth status

# Step 3: Activate your anchors
authpf-api-cli authpf activate

# Step 4: Check anchor status
authpf-api-cli authpf status

# Step 5: When done - deactivate anchors
authpf-api-cli authpf deactivate

# Step 6: Logout
authpf-api-cli auth logout
.EE

.SS Server Administrator Workflow
.EX
# Create a new user
authpf-api-cli user create --username john --password mypassword --role user

# Change a user's password
authpf-api-cli user modify --username john --password newpassword

# Promote user to admin
authpf-api-cli user modify --username john --role admin

# List all users
authpf-api-cli user list

# Delete a user
authpf-api-cli user delete --username john

# Display configuration
authpf-api-cli config show
.EE

.SS Advanced Usage
.EX
# Login with custom CA certificate
authpf-api-cli auth login --server https://api.example.com --username john --password pass -c /path/to/ca.crt

# Activate anchor for 2 hours
authpf-api-cli authpf activate -t 2h

# Activate another user's anchor (admin only)
authpf-api-cli authpf activate -u user2

# Check all active connections (admin only)
authpf-api-cli authpf status --all

# Deactivate all anchors (admin only)
authpf-api-cli authpf deactivate --all

# Verbose output for debugging
authpf-api-cli --verbose auth login --server https://api.example.com --username john --password pass
.EE

.SH FILES
.IP \(bu 2
\fB~/.authpf-api-cli/config\fR — Default configuration file
.IP \(bu 2
\fB~/.authpf-api-cli/credentials\fR — Credentials File (Username, Hashed Password)

.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\fBauthpf-api.conf(5)\fR — Configuration file for authpf-api

.SH HISTORY
\fBauthpf-api-cli\fP was created as a command-line interface to the \fBauthpf-api\fP server, providing both client-side operations (authentication, rule activation/deactivation) and server-side administration (user management, configuration).

